eived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2535,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-11-27T20:29:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-06T16:30:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T14:12:58Z","closed_at":"2026-05-14T14:12:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.6.stable.official\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot v4.6.stable - Forward+ - D3D12 driver\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe Godot editor crashes (process exits immediately, no error dialog, no entry in Output panel) when a `ShaderMaterial` is assigned a `.gdshader` whose `#include`d `.gdshaderinc` declares a function with a parameter whose name matches a `uniform` declared in the host shader.\n\nPer GLSL scoping rules, function parameters should locally shadow outer-scope identifiers without conflict. Other engines (and the GLSL spec) handle this correctly.\n\nThe issue was confirmed by controlled-variable testing: changing only the parameter name (with no other modification) toggles between \"crash on shader assignment\" and \"works correctly\" — 100% reproducible in both directions.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUsing the attached MRP:\n\n1. Open the project in Godot 4.6\n2. In FileSystem, right-click anywhere → **New Resource…** → search `ShaderMaterial` → Create → save as `test_mat.tres`\n3. Select the new resource. In the Inspector, click the **Shader** field's dropdown → **Quick Load** → select `test.gdshader`\n\n**Result: editor process terminates immediately with no error dialog.**\n\nTo confirm the bug is the parameter-shadow specifically, edit `style.gdshaderinc` and rename the parameter:\n\n```glsl\nvec3 tint(vec3 base_color) {\n    return base_color * 0.5;\n}\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[godot-shader-include-bug-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27448867/godot-shader-include-bug-mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119287/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119287/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}